Litematica Preview is a Windows port of LitematicaQL by Arcadi4.
Source baseline: 4bbeeae4ddfd5d4afa0280ba42f6a01bc8df7ab6.
The source repository's LICENSE is GNU AGPL version 3 and is preserved.
The source NOTICE described an older MIT license; this port follows LICENSE.

The material-replacement feature models the behavior of the SchematicPreview
mod by DimasKama (https://github.com/DimasKama/SchematicPreview). Only its
replace semantics were reimplemented in Mesher/src/replace.rs; no source code
was copied. SchematicPreview is proprietary ("All rights reserved").

Nucleation and schematic-mesher power file decoding and meshing.
Nucleation 0.10.14 is used unmodified from crates.io. Mesher/src/litematic.rs,
Mesher/src/schematic.rs and Mesher/src/meshing.rs contain application-owned
readers/adapters adapted from its MIT-licensed implementation (Copyright (c) 2025
Schem-at); the full license is in ThirdParty/Nucleation-LICENSE.txt.
schematic-mesher 0.2.0 is also used unmodified from crates.io. Mesher/src/meshing/
adapts its public builders for neighbor-aware chunks, stable texture atlases and
mesh buffer ownership. Its license is in ThirdParty/schematic-mesher-LICENSE.txt.
Tauri 2 provides the Rust desktop host and the Windows WebView2 integration.
React and Fluent UI React v9 provide the desktop interface and Fluent System Icons.
The preview renderer uses WebGL 2 and gl-matrix for camera and matrix operations.
The shipped app does not use .NET, OpenTK, GLFW, or a Node.js runtime.

See ThirdParty/ for bundled dependency license texts and dependency inventories.
The historical OpenTK and GLFW license files are retained as provenance; those
components are not part of the current executable. WebView2 is a separately
installed Microsoft runtime and remains subject to Microsoft's license terms.

